---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting Started — Awesome GitHub"
  description="Learn why .github matters, how to implement it, and the accessibility guidelines."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Getting Started</div>
    <h1>Build Your .github Control Plane</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything you need to understand, implement, and onboard your team to a .github-based governance system.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section quickstart">
    <h2>5-Minute Quickstart</h2>
    <div class="quickstart-box">
      <div class="step">
        <strong>Step 1: Clone the repository</strong>
        <code>git clone https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github.git</code>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <strong>Step 2: Install dependencies</strong>
        <code>npm install</code>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <strong>Step 3: Explore the structure</strong>
        <code>ls -la agents/ instructions/ hooks/ skills/</code>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <strong>Step 4: Read the introduction</strong>
        <p>
          Open <code>CLAUDE.md</code> and <code>AGENTS.md</code> for governance guidelines and AI rules.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <strong>Step 5: Explore one agent</strong>
        <p>
          Pick an agent from <code>agents/</code>, read its documentation, and understand its capabilities.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Learning Path</h2>
    <div class="learning-path">
      <article class="path-card">
        <div class="step-number">1</div>
        <h3>Why .github Matters</h3>
        <p>
          Understand the problem: Why teams struggle with fragmented governance, inconsistent
          automation, and delivery drift.
        </p>
        <a href="/getting-started/why-github-matters/" class="path-link">
          Learn →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card">
        <div class="step-number">2</div>
        <h3>Watch the Talk</h3>
        <p>
          See the full architecture, technical layers, and adoption playbook in the 25-minute WCEU 2026
          presentation.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slideshow/" class="path-link">
          Watch Presentation →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card">
        <div class="step-number">3</div>
        <h3>Explore Agent Guides</h3>
        <p>
          Meet the 6 core agents: Release, Branding, Meta, Linting, Labelling, and Planner. Learn their
          roles and how they integrate.
        </p>
        <a href="/agents/" class="path-link">
          Explore Agents →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card">
        <div class="step-number">4</div>
        <h3>Implementation Roadmap</h3>
        <p>
          Follow the 30/60/90 day adoption plan. Know which agents to adopt first, dependencies, and
          effort estimates.
        </p>
        <a href="/getting-started/implementation-roadmap/" class="path-link">
          View Roadmap →
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Key Topics</h2>
    <div class="topic-grid">
      <article class="topic-card">
        <h3>Architecture</h3>
        <p>
          Learn about the control plane architecture: how governance files, reusable workflows, agents,
          skills, and hooks fit together.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slides/4/" class="inline-link">View in Slide 4 →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="topic-card">
        <h3>Governance Model</h3>
        <p>
          Understand the policy and instruction hierarchy that governs AI operations and ensures
          accountability.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slides/19/" class="inline-link">View in Slide 19 →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="topic-card">
        <h3>Lessons & Patterns</h3>
        <p>
          Learn from hard-won experience: what works, what doesn't, and common pitfalls to avoid.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slides/11/" class="inline-link">View in Slide 11 →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="topic-card">
        <h3>Adoption Playbook</h3>
        <p>
          Get a practical implementation sequence your teams can follow. Start with one outcome, roll
          out gradually.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slides/12/" class="inline-link">View in Slide 12 →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Quick Reference</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/talk/">Talk Overview</a> — 25-minute presentation on .github governance
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/talk/slides/">All Slides</a> — Browse the 20 slides individually
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/agents/">Agent Guides</a> — Explore each of the 6 core agents
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/references/glossary/">Glossary</a> — Key terminology and definitions
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/references/sources/">Sources & Tools</a> — Evidence and reference materials
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .quickstart {
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary, #f6f8fa);
  }

  .quickstart-box {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .step {
    background: white;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary, #0969da);
  }

  .step strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .step code {
    display: block;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary, #f6f8fa);
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-family: "Courier New", monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .step p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .learning-path {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .path-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    position: relative;
  }

  .step-number {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .path-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .path-card p {
    flex: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .path-link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: all 0.2s ease-out;
  }

  .path-link:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .topic-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .topic-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .topic-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .topic-card p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .learning-path,
    .topic-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
